{"parseRefreshTokenResponse writes a literal string 'refresh_token' when the response lacks a refresh token, which can be persisted to the DB and break future refreshes by overwriting the real refresh token with an invalid placeholder": 0.9558190107345581, "parseRefreshTokenResponse declares a Zod object using computed keys derived from Zod schemas (.toString()), which is not a valid way to express dynamic keys and will fail at build/runtime": 0.9005910158157349, "parseRefreshTokenResponse returns a SafeParseReturnType object ({success, data}), but the Google Calendar code saves this entire wrapper as the credential key, corrupting the database record": 0.9634642004966736, "When credential sync is enabled, refreshOAuthTokens returns a native fetch Response which has no .data property, but Google Calendar code accesses res?.data expecting a GaxiosResponse structure": 0.9617499113082886, "SalesforceCalendarService calls prisma.credential.update without importing prisma, causing a compile-time failure": 0.3331340551376343, "SalesforceCalendarService constructs the jsforce.Connection using the pre-refresh access token from credentialKey instead of the newly refreshed token": 0.8907747864723206, "The app-credential webhook does not restrict HTTP methods and uses zod.parse + decrypt + JSON.parse without handling errors, so malformed but authenticated requests will return 500s instead of 4xx": 0.9430594444274902, "APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is assigned the raw env var string(s) rather than a boolean, which can lead to accidental misuse and increases the risk of leaking secret values if ever logged or serialized": 0.8166608810424805, "In BiginCalendarService.refreshAccessToken, credentialId (the database credential primary key) is passed as the userId parameter to refreshOAuthTokens instead of credential.userId": 0.9879432320594788, "parseRefreshTokenResponse throws on validation failure instead of returning {success: false}, but Zoom and Salesforce check !parsedToken.success after the call - this is dead code since the throw prevents reaching those checks": 0.8387409448623657}